{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a photoinduced decarboxylative alkynylation of redox-active esters (RAEs) using inexpensive copper catalysts (CuCl and Cu(acac)2) and blue LED irradiation. The method allows for the coupling of primary, secondary, and tertiary alkyl radicals derived from carboxylic acids with both aryl and aliphatic alkynes. Key findings include the critical role of the bidentate acetylacetonate ligand in inhibiting alkyne homo-coupling and the use of copper-phenylacetylide as a photocatalyst for non-aryl alkynes.",
